Varda Burstyn, editor.  Women against censorship.  Douglas & McIntyre,
Vancouver, 1985. Review: The book is a collection of essays by various fem-
inists who are opposed to censorship and to the anti-pornography movement
represented by Andrea Dworkin and Catherine MacKinnon. The women who
have contributed essays to the book have in common only their devotion to
feminism and their opposition to censorship. They state reasons for opposi-
tion which come from several different viewpoints. If you have an interest in
opposing the public control of ideas, in whatever form it might take, I highly
recommend the book. - Joseph F. Mays, joemays@bsu-cs.bsu.edu Excerpts:
enclosed.

